"""
The vault command of Wolly: converts a vault of Wolly.Vault into one of Standard.Vault.

    vault convert OLD_VAULT OLD_KEY NEW_ENV NEW_PEPPER KEY_NAME

It takes paths and the name of the key line, never a secret: the secrets are read from the old
vault with its key and written into the new one, each read back and compared.  It prints the
number of secrets converted and every name refused (a name that starts with a digit, which
Standard.Vault does not take), and exits 0; it prints why not and exits 1 when there is no old
vault at its path (nothing is written then), it does not open under its key, or the new one cannot
be written.  The old files stay; the caller removes
them after.
"""
module Wolly.Example.VaultCommand is
    """
    The command of the arguments.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    function main(root: RootCapability): ExitCode;
end module.
